WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.021 --> 00:00:15.788
"I a confession to make," Luke went on.

2
00:00:15.808 --> 00:00:17.489
"I knew it!"

3
00:00:17.789 --> 00:00:18.670
Maggie exclaimed.

4
00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:21.011
"You took those tickets, didn't you?"

5
00:00:21.031 --> 00:00:24.173
"What?" Luke looked confused.

6
00:00:24.193 --> 00:00:25.453
"No, wait.

7
00:00:25.874 --> 00:00:29.476
My confession is that I already saw Revenge of the Pirate's Ghost.

8
00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:32.617
My uncle owns a movie theater in my hometown.

9
00:00:33.258 --> 00:00:35.319
He held an early screening, and I got to go."

10
00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:37.600
Henry was surprised.

11
00:00:38.181 --> 00:00:40.102
That wasn't the confession he'd expected!

12
00:00:40.122 --> 00:00:42.323
"Wait," Henry said.

13
00:00:42.343 --> 00:00:44.864
"You already saw the movie?

14
00:00:45.205 --> 00:00:46.265
Why didn't you tell us?"

15
00:00:47.306 --> 00:00:48.026
Luke shrugged.

16
00:00:48.046 --> 00:00:51.288
"I didn't want to give away any secrets about the plot.

17
00:00:52.389 --> 00:00:57.332
Especially anything important, like Captain Green is actually the main pirate's brother Oops!"

18
00:00:58.496 --> 00:01:00.218
He clapped one hand over his mouth.

19
00:01:01.018 --> 00:01:02.920
Then he pulled it away, looking sheepish.

20
00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.902
"Don't tell Nathan I just said that, okay?

21
00:01:06.523 --> 00:01:08.364
He's really excited to see the movie.

22
00:01:09.405 --> 00:01:11.166
I don't want to ruin the surprise for him.

23
00:01:11.927 --> 00:01:13.768
Sorry I just ruined it for you guys."

24
00:01:13.788 --> 00:01:20.554
"It's okay, and don't worry, we won't tell Nathan," Cole promised while Henry and Maggie nodded.

25
00:01:20.574 --> 00:01:23.456
"But does this mean you didn't take our booty?"

26
00:01:23.476 --> 00:01:25.057
"Of course not!"

27
00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:25.998
Luke said.

28
00:01:26.018 --> 00:01:28.060
"Why would I do that?

29
00:01:28.484 --> 00:01:29.224
I'm not a thief."

30
00:01:31.025 --> 00:01:32.586
He hurried to rejoin the others.

31
00:01:33.527 --> 00:01:35.027
Henry looked at Maggie and Cole.

32
00:01:36.168 --> 00:01:38.169
"I guess Luke's innocent," he said.

33
00:01:38.189 --> 00:01:42.951
"If he already saw that movie, he has no motive for stealing the tickets."

34
00:01:44.012 --> 00:01:45.512
"Yeah," Maggie agreed.

35
00:01:45.532 --> 00:01:48.534
"Especially since his uncle owns a movie theater.

36
00:01:49.374 --> 00:01:51.295
He can see any movie whenever he wants."

37
00:01:56.328 --> 00:01:59.750
A few minutes later the whole group reached the town of Sea Cove.

38
00:02:00.911 --> 00:02:03.892
Maggie hurried over to Anna and Luke, who were looking at the drawing.

39
00:02:04.793 --> 00:02:06.353
Cole was about to go over there too.

40
00:02:06.954 --> 00:02:08.114
But Henry grabbed his arm.

41
00:02:09.175 --> 00:02:11.676
"Look," he said, pointing to a shop nearby.

42
00:02:11.696 --> 00:02:16.639
"Sea Cove General Store," Cole said, reading the sign on the front.

43
00:02:16.659 --> 00:02:19.260
"That must be Anna's family's store."

44
00:02:20.381 --> 00:02:22.122
"That's not all," Henry said.

45
00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:27.597
"Look at the initials—SCGS.

46
00:02:27.657 --> 00:02:29.498
That's where Roger got that soda cup.

47
00:02:29.878 --> 00:02:30.839
Let's go find out!"

48
00:02:32.501 --> 00:02:33.762
They hurried toward the store.

49
00:02:34.542 --> 00:02:37.505
When they got closer, Henry could see it wasn't just a store.

50
00:02:38.385 --> 00:02:41.788
There was a sandwich shop, a catering business, and a soda fountain.

51
00:02:41.808 --> 00:02:46.672
"Wow, Anna's family sure must be busy," he commented.

52
00:02:47.733 --> 00:02:48.734
Cole didn't answer.

53
00:02:49.414 --> 00:02:51.016
He was looking in another direction.

54
00:02:51.036 --> 00:02:52.497
"Here comes William."

55
00:02:53.538 --> 00:02:55.640
Henry looked and saw William walking toward them.

56
00:02:56.744 --> 00:03:00.367
"Let's try to question him while he's alone," he whispered to Cole.

57
00:03:01.567 --> 00:03:03.689
When William got closer, Henry smiled.

58
00:03:03.709 --> 00:03:05.390
"Hi, William.

59
00:03:06.171 --> 00:03:08.012
Are your new shoes more comfortable?"

60
00:03:08.392 --> 00:03:08.853
he said.

61
00:03:09.873 --> 00:03:11.554
They all looked down at William's feet.

62
00:03:12.215 --> 00:03:14.917
He was wearing the same shoes he'd had on all day.

63
00:03:14.937 --> 00:03:18.939
"I couldn't find my other sandals," William mumbled.

64
00:03:18.959 --> 00:03:21.301
"So I just left these on."

65
00:03:21.321 --> 00:03:24.343
"Are you sure that's what happened?"

66
00:03:24.663 --> 00:03:25.224
Cole said.

67
00:03:26.328 --> 00:03:29.431
"Or were you really hiding something in your room?"

68
00:03:29.451 --> 00:03:31.613
"Hiding something?

69
00:03:32.053 --> 00:03:32.914
What do you mean?"

70
00:03:33.355 --> 00:03:34.115
William asked.

71
00:03:35.236 --> 00:03:36.297
Henry elbowed Cole.

72
00:03:36.978 --> 00:03:39.260
Henry didn't want Cole to give away their suspicions.

73
00:03:40.161 --> 00:03:41.322
But Cole ignored him.

74
00:03:41.342 --> 00:03:43.624
"Did you take those movie tickets, William?"

75
00:03:44.825 --> 00:03:46.746
"What?" William looked confused.

76
00:03:46.766 --> 00:03:48.348
"Of course not!

77
00:03:48.708 --> 00:03:49.809
Why would I do that?"

78
00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:52.892
"We don't know," Henry spoke up.

79
00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:56.941
"But we've noticed that you don't seem very happy to have us here.

80
00:03:57.762 --> 00:04:00.083
Maybe you changed your mind about inviting us."

81
00:04:01.383 --> 00:04:02.684
"Yeah," Cole added.

82
00:04:02.704 --> 00:04:06.385
"Maybe you're trying to ruin the treasure hunt so we'll leave early."

83
00:04:07.306 --> 00:04:08.346
William looked upset.

84
00:04:09.106 --> 00:04:09.907
"No way!"

85
00:04:10.267 --> 00:04:10.987
he blurted out.

86
00:04:11.007 --> 00:04:13.248
"I'm glad you guys are here!"

87
00:04:13.268 --> 00:04:16.830
"Then why have you been in such a bad mood all day?"

88
00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:17.930
Cole asked.

89
00:04:19.171 --> 00:04:20.731
William sighed.

90
00:04:21.171 --> 00:04:22.112
"Sorry about that.

91
00:04:22.888 --> 00:04:24.089
It's because of my parents.

92
00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:28.432
They're used to spending lots of money entertaining people for Dad's job.

93
00:04:29.533 --> 00:04:31.554
I didn't want them to do that this weekend.

94
00:04:32.355 --> 00:04:35.176
I just wanted us to have a fun, normal weekend at the beach."

95
00:04:35.717 --> 00:04:36.337
He shrugged.

96
00:04:36.998 --> 00:04:40.260
"But they planned this whole expensive treasure hunt without even telling me!

97
00:04:41.301 --> 00:04:43.222
I was afraid you'd all think I was showing off."

98
00:04:43.242 --> 00:04:46.024
"Is that why you kept disappearing?"

99
00:04:46.344 --> 00:04:47.104
Cole asked.

100
00:04:48.225 --> 00:04:49.006
William nodded.

101
00:04:49.026 --> 00:04:52.028
"I was trying to get them to tell me what else they have planned.

102
00:04:52.812 --> 00:04:54.312
But they wouldn't tell me anything."

103
00:04:55.333 --> 00:04:57.373
Henry could tell William was being truthful.

104
00:04:57.393 --> 00:04:58.894
"Don't worry.

105
00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:00.834
We didn't think you were showing off."

106
00:05:00.854 --> 00:05:04.495
"Yeah. The treasure hunt is fantastic."

107
00:05:06.416 --> 00:05:07.936
Cole clapped William on the shoulder.

108
00:05:07.956 --> 00:05:10.957
"Anyway, we like you no matter what."

109
00:05:11.977 --> 00:05:12.677
Henry nodded.

110
00:05:12.697 --> 00:05:16.258
"We don't care how much money your parents spend," he added.

111
00:05:16.278 --> 00:05:19.079
"We came because you're our friend."

112
00:05:20.259 --> 00:05:21.320
William looked relieved.

113
00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:27.186
"Thanks. In that case I'll be in a better mood from now on," he promised.

114
00:05:27.206 --> 00:05:30.128
"Good." Henry smiled.

115
00:05:30.608 --> 00:05:31.949
Then he realized something.

116
00:05:31.969 --> 00:05:35.831
"This means we still don't know who took those tickets."

117
00:05:36.951 --> 00:05:38.812
"Is Roger Redbeard still a suspect?"

118
00:05:39.152 --> 00:05:39.913
William asked.

119
00:05:39.933 --> 00:05:45.416
"Because when I was leaving my house just now, I saw him lurking around outside!"
